+// the token_embd rows listed in output_ids, so a token inside the head can be read from RAM instead of faulting its
+// row in from flash through the lazily mapped token_embd. The head is either plain (CPU / mmap buffer: rows are
+// contiguous) or a Q4_K head repacked by the CPU backend into 8-row interleaved blocks (block_q4_Kx8, row count a
+// multiple of 8): then a row is rebuilt as plain Q4_K blocks (inverse of make_block_q4_Kx8; the interleave, 4 or 8
+// bytes, depends on the CPU and is found by the check). Checked once per head: 8 rows rebuilt and compared byte for
+// byte with token_embd; an untied head (9B) or rows quantized differently fall back to the stock GET_ROWS.
+// LLAMA_EMBD_FROM_HEAD=0 = off.
+struct tv_head_embd_map {
+    bool ok = false;
+    int  il = 0;              // 0 = plain rows, 4 / 8 = Q4_Kx8 repack with that interleave
+    std::vector<int32_t> inv; // vocab id -> head row, -1 = not in head
